On Sat, Oct 30, 2010 at 12:39 PM, Calpin <calumhalpin@googlemail.com> wrote:
>
> What I meant was that L4B seemed to be saying that "pu", "ca" and "ba"
> and 2 sumti where x1 was an event and x2 was another event before,
> simultaneously or after respectively.

Where does L4B seem to say that?.

>Are you saying that it instead
> adds x1 to an existing bridi which would act as x2?

It adds an additional (unnumbered) place to the existing places of a
selbri. There are no x1 or x2 involved.

> If that is the case, can they be placed anywhere in the bridi

Yes.

> e.g. "mi
> klama le mi zdani ba mi tavla do" (apologies if this is incorrect in
> some other way, hopefully it gets my thinking across)?

It has to be:

    mi klama le mi zdani ba lo nu mi tavla do

After "ba" you need a sumti. The way you had it the sumti after "ba"
is "mi", and then comes a separate selbri "tavla" that has nothing to
do because we already have a selbri ("klama") in our main bridi. With
"ba" we are adding an unnumbered argument place to "klama".

> L4B seemed to
> be saying that they had to be placed at the beginning of a bridi or
> right before the selbri e.g. "ba mi tavla do ku mi klama le mi
> zdani" / "mi ba klama le mi zdani".

Right before the selbri and without a sumti is fine.

At the beginning of the bridi is also fine, but you need to follow it
with a sumti, so:

   ba (lo (nu (mi tavla do vau) kei) ku) mi klama le mi zdani

(Only one of the terminators is actually required.)

You can also omit the sumti, but then you need to terminate it with
"ku", so it won't grab the next sumti:

  (ba ku) mi klama le mi zdani
  "Later, I go to my house."

mu'o mi'e xorxes

